# per-worktree agent briefing and investigation scratch (.handover/ROLE.md,
# fixtures pulled for local runs, probe scripts). Never meant to be committed -
# ignored so that a `git add -A` cannot sweep it into a commit.
.handover/

# The effects v3 conformance corpus is checked in deliberately. The *.hex rule
# above comes from the C/C++ template, where .hex means a compiled firmware
# image; these are test fixtures and are the shared statement of the wire
# format, so they must be tracked.
!tests/fixtures/effects_v3/*.hex
